description:
The subject who owns this power has a deep affiliation with visual arts, so deep that he/she can acquire a superpower every time he/she admires or looks at an artwork. The power he/she obtains depends from:

1. The subject of the artwork;
2. The feeling that the artist is trying to get viewers to experience;
3. The subjective perspective of the owner. 

Some examples: Michelangelo's David can give an extraordinary aim, Guernica gives the possibility of instill paranoic desperation into s. O, et
